 "intro": "Near Pistoria in Etruria, January 62 BC. Catiline, whose conspiracy against the Republic was exposed by Cicero, is trying to escape over the Apennines with about 3,000 men. You command the government army under Marcus Petreius, in place of the consul Antonius, who claims to have gout.",
 "debrief": "In Sallust’s account, Catiline was trapped between Metellus Celer, holding the passes, and the army of Antonius under Petreius. He fought in a narrow valley, having sent away the horses. Petreius put his veteran cohorts in front, then sent his praetorian cohort through the rebel centre. Catiline charged into the Roman ranks and died; Sallust says none of his men was taken alive, and all lay where they had fought. The victors found friends and kin among the dead. The other choices are what-ifs.",
